tiring:
At hoping I should learn to write your notes
And save the tiring of your eyes, at night;
And most for that sweet thrice you kissed my lips

tireless:
All that was drunken once with light and air;
The earth will not regret her tireless lover,
Nor he awake to know she does not care.

tire:
Diviner summits to attain,
With faith that sinks and feet that tire;
But nought shall conquer or control
